{
  "info": {
    "name": "Week 4 - Social Feed API (capstone)",
    "description": "SkillNexis Week 4 capstone. The React client calls exactly these routes.\n\nRun top to bottom: 'Register Alice' and 'Register Bob' save their tokens into {{token}} and {{otherToken}}, and the post requests save ids into {{postId}} and {{otherPostId}}.\n\nThings worth noticing while running it:\n- reading is public (the timeline, a profile and a comment thread all work with the Authorization header removed), but writing is not;\n- likes and follows are toggles - send them twice and you are back where you started;\n- a comment can be removed by the person who wrote it AND by whoever owns the post it sits under, but by nobody else;\n- deleting a post takes its likes, its comments and its image with it.\n\nThe two upload requests need a file picked by hand in Postman (Body > form-data), since a collection cannot carry one.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
